  "text": "A set of questions meant to gauge overall mental ability, knowledge of mechanical principles, and emotional stability was taken from a revised series of a motor‑vehicle assessment created by a Midwestern university. These items were given to 220 participants who were enrolled in a nationwide public‑works program. The participants represented adults with a range of schooling levels, allowing comparison of how educational background relates to performance on the three types of mental tasks. Results showed how general intelligence, mechanical understanding, and personality balance varied among the different educational groups."
